FAIL: the vendor billed 506, our ledger charged -76,
and 140 of the difference is known CI spend. 442 credits are UNEXPLAINED —
they reached the provider without reaching a counter. Both guards
degrade OPEN — consumeOddsCredit returns true when FIELD_JOURNALISM is unbound,
checkAndIncrementDailyOdds returns true on any KV error — so spend that the
vendor saw and we did not is the signature of a guard that stopped guarding.
This compares the two counters to EACH OTHER, so it is not the standing
cumulative gap (19,582 on 2026-09-16); it is new divergence in this interval.

COVERAGE: 14 progress rows since 2026-09-04, 9 provider reading(s).
odds_backfill_progress is keyed by DATE, so a date mixing a paired sport with an
unpaired one reads as paired — this catches total failure per date, not per sport.
KNOWN CI SPEND IS A LOWER BOUND: only odds-backfill records its own credits, so
probes and one-off fills are NOT subtracted and UNEXPLAINED is an upper bound on
real leakage. Joined on completed_at (the run clock), never on date (the day
being backfilled) — a run today writes yesterday's row.
